h2 id="ai-assisted-production">AI-assisted production</h2><p>Parts of the site&rsquo;s production workflow are automated and may use AI-assisted generation.</p><p>Automation does not lower our quality standard. Generated material is processed through validation and publishing checks intended to reduce:</p><ul><li>Repetition</li><li>Formatting errors</li><li>Weak structure</li><li>Metadata problems</li><li>Image problems</li><li>Inconsistent categories</li><li>Broken links</li></ul><p>The publishing system is continuously improved as problems are discovered.</p><h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2><p>If we discover that an article contains an error, outdated information, a broken link, or another quality problem, we aim to correct it. Readers can report problems through the Contact page.</p><h2 id="our-editorial-principle">Our editorial principle</h2><p>The simplest useful answer is usually better than a complicated answer that does not help the reader act.</p><p>We aim for practical, clear, honest, and useful content.</p>
